       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks wrong. **Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose.**\n\n- The usual adult dose is 5 mg once daily, sometimes 2.5 mg to start.\n- The maximum is 10 mg once daily.\n- At 50 mg, you'd expect severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and possibly shock. Amlodipine stays in the body a long time (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours), so an overdose can last for days.\n\nThis could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is the most common starting dose. Can you confirm what you meant? For example:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**\n3. Something else\n\nAs soon as you confirm, I'll enter the order."
