     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered it. I'm not able to place amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. There's no recognized clinical reason to give more than 10 mg a day, and 50 mg is in the range where overdoses cause long-lasting shock that's hard to reverse. Because this would go straight to administration, the risk to the patient is too high to proceed on my end.\n\nYour \"Yes, I confirm\" may have been meant for one of the options I listed. If so, tell me which one and I'll enter it right away:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily** (usual starting dose)\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** (maximum dose)\n\nIf you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I can help enter a second medication instead, such as an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide.\n\nIf you're sure 50 mg is intended for a specific reason, please talk to the pharmacist or attending and use the order system's override process. That way the order gets the independent review that a dose this high needs."
      }
     ],
